<title>AUSTRALIA: AWB Australia wheat indicator prices-April 18.</title>
<headline>AWB Australia wheat indicator prices-April 18.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Wheat Board international card prices for wheat exports for April 18.</p>
<p>In U.S. dollars per tonne, FOB eastern states.</p>
<p>		ASW	  AH    PH 13 PCT  PH 14 PCT</p>
<p>    Apr    221.50    225.00    225.50     230.50</p>
<p>    May    221.50    225.00    225.50     230.50</p>
<p>    Jun    218.50    222.00    222.50     229.00</p>
<p>    Jul    214.50    218.00    218.50     226.50</p>
<p>    Aug    213.50    217.00    217.50     225.50</p>
<p>    Sept   213.50    217.00    217.50     225.50</p>
<p>Note: ASW = Australian Standard White; AH = Australian Hard; PH = Australian Prime Hard; percentages = protein content.</p>
<p>Australian Wheat Board indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1997/98 crop wheat increased A$6.00 per tonne.</p>
<p>	  Indicator Prices in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		  ASW 10 pct protein</p>
<p>    National FOB	195.00</p>
<p>Indicator prices on a delivered port basis:</p>
<p> Queensland			   South Australia</p>
<p>    Mackay	  170.50	    Port Adelaide	 172.00</p>
<p>    Gladstone     170.75	    Port Giles	    172.75</p>
<p>    Brisbane	168.50	    Wallaroo		170.50</p>
<p> New South Wales			Port Pirie	    167.50</p>
<p>    Newcastle     170.50	    Port Lincoln	  173.75</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   171.00	    Thevenard	     168.75</p>
<p>Victoria			     Western Australia</p>
<p>    Geelong	 170.00	     Esperance	    175.25</p>
<p>    Portland	171.00	     Albany		 176.25</p>
<p>					     Fremantle	    178.25</p>
<p>					     Geraldton	    176.25</p>
<p>NOTE: The indicator price represents the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract fob price quoted on a delivered port basis, offered today by the AWB for wheat delivered during the 1997/98 harvest. The offer is valid until 4.30 p.m. Australian Eastern Standard Time (0630 GMT).  </p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
